318
00:13:29.150 --> 00:13:31.750
Well, do you remember the summer my hair turned green?
那么，你还记得我头发变绿的那年夏天吗？

319
00:13:32.010 --> 00:13:32.210
Yep.
记得。

320
00:13:32.670 --> 00:13:33.930
You could really see it on camera.
在镜头里真的看得很清楚。

321
00:13:34.090 --> 00:13:37.430
Guys, I spent the whole summer swimming with the kids in the pool and my hair turned green.
伙计们，我整个夏天都在泳池里陪孩子游泳，结果我的头发变绿了。

322
00:13:37.590 --> 00:13:40.050
It happens to the blondies out there.
金发女郎们经常遇到这种事。

323
00:13:40.550 --> 00:13:45.630
And Kim put this thing on my hair to like kind of tint it, you know?
然后金在我的头发上抹了点东西来染色，你知道的吧？

324
00:13:45.770 --> 00:13:46.690
To get the green out?
为了去除绿色？

325
00:13:46.690 --> 00:13:47.750
To get the green out.
为了去除绿色。

326
00:13:48.170 --> 00:13:50.210
And I had to wash it out of my hair.
我得把它从头发上洗掉。

327
00:13:50.390 --> 00:13:53.610
Like you put it on and then I had to rinse it out and then she had to blow dry my hair.
就像是你抹上它，然后我得把它冲洗干净，接着她得帮我用吹风机吹干头发。

328
00:13:53.910 --> 00:13:54.230
Okay.
好吧。

329
00:13:54.310 --> 00:13:59.390
Now, why didn't they just use the little sink in the hair and makeup trailer or the shower in your trailer?
话说回来，为什么他们不直接用美发化妆车里的小洗手盆，或者是你房车里的淋浴间呢？

330
00:14:00.170 --> 00:14:04.450
Because the sink in the hair and makeup trailer, first of all, it didn't get hot.
因为美发化妆车里的洗手盆，首先，水一点也不热。

331
00:14:05.170 --> 00:14:10.090
And Kim was a little concerned because the water is like this sort of recycled water.
而且金有点担心，因为那水是那种循环水。

332
00:14:10.330 --> 00:14:10.570
Yes.
是的。

333
00:14:10.570 --> 00:14:14.430
That it would strip the color off my hair that she was trying to put in.
担心它会洗掉她刚努力染在我头发上的颜色。

334
00:14:14.430 --> 00:14:20.710
Now that you say that, I know that because there have been times when I've needed to shower off.
经你这么一说，我明白了，因为有时候我也需要洗个澡。

335
00:14:21.050 --> 00:14:24.510
Your trailers have a shower, but it is exactly that.
你们的房车里确实有淋浴间，但情况正是如此。

336
00:14:24.650 --> 00:14:28.190
It's like a tank of weird sort of chemically treated water.
它就像是一个装满了某种经过化学处理的怪异水的储水箱。

337
00:14:28.370 --> 00:14:28.570
Right.
没错。

338
00:14:28.750 --> 00:14:31.730
So that it can stay in the tank and then not be poisonous.
这样水就能储存在箱子里，而且不会有毒。

339
00:14:32.130 --> 00:14:32.270
Yeah.
是啊。

340
00:14:32.710 --> 00:14:34.530
And it doesn't get very hot.
而且水温一点也不热。

341
00:14:34.830 --> 00:14:38.290
And also, I've had people tell me not to use it.
另外，也有人提醒过我不要用。

342
00:14:38.390 --> 00:14:42.110
I sort of was like, maybe just get rid of the showers and the trailers.
我当时就觉得，也许应该把房车里的淋浴间拆了。

343
00:14:42.310 --> 00:14:42.930
Yeah, put in a closet.
对，改成衣橱。

344
00:14:42.930 --> 00:14:43.530
They're taking up space.
它们太占空间了。

345
00:14:43.530 --> 00:14:44.950
We all need a closet.
我们都需要一个衣橱。

346
00:14:45.230 --> 00:14:46.490
Always need more closet.
永远都需要更多的衣橱。

347
00:14:46.690 --> 00:14:48.210
I mean, it's part of my life mantra.
我的意思是，这是我的人生格言的一部分。

348
00:14:48.410 --> 00:14:49.430
Can I have more closets?
我能拥有更多衣橱吗？

349
00:14:51.010 --> 00:14:53.590
Well, you need closets for your baskets, ladies.
女士们，你们确实需要衣橱来放你们的篮子。

350
00:14:53.730 --> 00:14:54.090
I do.
我确实需要。

351
00:14:54.090 --> 00:14:55.030
Your basket collection.
你的篮子收藏。

352
00:14:55.150 --> 00:14:56.170
Give me all the baskets.
把所有的篮子都给我。

353
00:14:56.470 --> 00:15:01.290
Well, listen, this little room, it was located in our writer's building.
听着，这个小房间，它在我们编剧大楼里。

354
00:15:01.970 --> 00:15:03.750
It was on the bottom floor.
它在底层。

355
00:15:04.190 --> 00:15:07.470
And it was an actual storage closet.
而且它真的是个储藏室。

356
00:15:07.470 --> 00:15:10.930
It was not a set, so the walls did not move.
它不是布景，所以墙壁是不能移动的。

357
00:15:11.190 --> 00:15:15.450
They talked about, should we build Michael Scott Paper Company in the warehouse?
他们讨论过，我们应该把迈克尔·斯科特纸业公司建在仓库里吗？

358
00:15:15.570 --> 00:15:16.670
That was my thought.
那是我的想法。

359
00:15:16.930 --> 00:15:18.710
Where we've built many a set.
我们在那里搭过许多布景。

360
00:15:19.190 --> 00:15:19.750
No.
没有。

361
00:15:19.750 --> 00:15:26.570
For whatever reason, they crammed us into the post-production storage room where, previous
不管出于什么原因，他们把我们塞进了后期制作储藏室，在那之前

362
00:15:26.570 --> 00:15:33.230
to us shooting in there, they had stored thousands of hours of archived tape of our show.
我们在那里拍摄之前，他们在那儿存放了我们节目数千小时的归档磁带。

363
00:15:33.230 --> 00:15:41.170
This was back in the day, and we just had walls and walls of five seasons of tape on our show.
那是过去的事了，我们节目有五季节目的磁带，墙上叠着墙。

364
00:15:41.450 --> 00:15:43.570
They had to relocate all the tapes.
他们不得不把所有的磁带都搬走。

365
00:15:43.750 --> 00:15:45.370
They had to redress the room.
他们不得不重新布置这个房间。

366
00:15:46.060 --> 00:15:49.270
I said, the shower is fake, but those pipes were real.
我说，淋浴是假的，但那些管道是真的。

367
00:15:49.450 --> 00:15:51.570
There really were these giant pipes.
真的有这些巨大的管道。

368
00:15:51.770 --> 00:15:54.650
Yes, the big black pipes that were coming out, those were real.
是的，那些伸出来的大黑管是真的。

369
00:15:54.890 --> 00:15:55.250
Yes.
是的。

370
00:15:56.010 --> 00:16:02.810
Also, the bathrooms that are outside in the hallway, the two doors on either side of the Michael Scott Paper Company door,
还有，走廊外面的洗手间，迈克尔·斯科特纸业公司门两侧的那两扇门，

371
00:16:03.070 --> 00:16:04.350
those bathrooms were real.
那些洗手间是真的。

372
00:16:04.730 --> 00:16:08.870
Those were the actual working bathrooms for anybody who worked on the bottom floor.
那是为任何在底层工作的人准备的真正可以使用的洗手间。

373
00:16:09.050 --> 00:16:12.550
Those were the bathrooms we would use in between scenes when we filmed in the warehouse.
那是我们在仓库拍摄时，在场景间隙会使用的洗手间。

374
00:16:12.710 --> 00:16:12.930
Yes.
是的。

375
00:16:13.170 --> 00:16:14.890
Or in that hallway by the editing bay.
或者在剪辑室旁边的那个走廊里。

376
00:16:14.890 --> 00:16:20.250
Right across from us were our two editors, Claire and Dave.
正对我们的是我们的两位剪辑师，克莱尔和戴夫。

377
00:16:20.590 --> 00:16:24.510
And above us were the writers' offices.
在我们上面是编剧办公室。

378
00:16:24.850 --> 00:16:27.550
So we were over in that building with the writers.
所以我们和编剧们在那栋楼里。

379
00:16:27.830 --> 00:16:32.630
Also in this building is the lobby area that leads out into the parking lot.
这栋楼里还有通往停车场的大堂区域。

380
00:16:33.090 --> 00:16:35.930
This room also gets repurposed for Cafe Disco.
这个房间后来也被改造成了迪斯科咖啡厅。

381
00:16:36.090 --> 00:16:36.450
Yes.
是的。

382
00:16:36.470 --> 00:16:38.190
We went back down there for that.
我们为了那个又回到了那里。

383
00:16:38.590 --> 00:16:40.630
So those are all my details on that room.
这就是我关于那个房间的所有细节。

384
00:16:40.630 --> 00:16:43.130
I'll have more to share as we break down the episode.
随着我们对这一集的剖析，我会有更多内容要分享。

385
00:16:43.130 --> 00:16:45.310
More little quirks of working in there.
更多在那里工作的小怪癖。

386
00:16:45.610 --> 00:16:47.230
Yeah, you spent a lot of time in there.
是啊，你在那里花了很多时间。

387
00:16:47.310 --> 00:16:47.710
We did.
我们确实如此。

388
00:16:48.170 --> 00:16:50.330
Are you ready for fast fact number two?
你准备好听第二个快速事实了吗？

389
00:16:50.550 --> 00:16:51.190
I am.
我准备好了。

390
00:16:51.690 --> 00:16:58.730
Remember last week when I told you that Michael sent a letter to everybody through NBC.com?
还记得上周我告诉你迈克尔通过 NBC.com 给每个人发了一封信吗？

391
00:16:58.770 --> 00:16:58.950
Yes.
记得。

392
00:16:59.110 --> 00:17:00.770
Announcing his new paper company?
宣布他成立了新的纸业公司？

393
00:17:00.770 --> 00:17:14.190
Well, this week he unveiled his website and NBC created a Michael Scott paper company website and it had photos of the room.
嗯，这周他公布了他的网站，NBC 创建了一个迈克尔·斯科特纸业公司网站，上面有那个房间的照片。

394
00:17:14.190 --> 00:17:17.730
It was basically the same room taken from three different angles.
基本上就是从三个不同角度拍的同一个房间。

395
00:17:18.050 --> 00:17:23.070
It had the downloadable coupon that is shown in this episode.
上面有本集里展示的可下载优惠券。

396
00:17:23.070 --> 00:17:26.550
You know, the one that promises unparalleled customer service.
你知道的，就是那张承诺无与伦比的客户服务的优惠券。

397
00:17:26.770 --> 00:17:26.890
Yep.
没错。

398
00:17:27.070 --> 00:17:29.430
That Pam and Ryan refused to copy.
潘和瑞安拒绝复印的那张。

399
00:17:29.430 --> 00:17:34.570
And it also had the mission statement for Michael Scott paper company.
上面还有迈克尔·斯科特纸业公司的使命宣言。

400
00:17:35.110 --> 00:17:36.050
Yes, it did.
是的，确实有。

401
00:17:36.050 --> 00:17:37.710
And we reached out to Joya.
而且我们联系了乔亚。

402
00:17:37.810 --> 00:17:39.170
You know, we've talked about Joya before.
你知道的，我们之前谈论过乔亚。

403
00:17:39.330 --> 00:17:45.170
She was in charge of all the digital content for the office that was on NBC.com.
她负责 NBC.com 上办公室的所有数字内容。

404
00:17:45.570 --> 00:17:48.310
She shared with us what the mission statement said.
她与我们分享了使命宣言的内容。

405
00:17:49.130 --> 00:17:50.030
Here it is.
就是这个。

406
00:17:50.030 --> 00:17:58.610
It's the Michael Scott paper company's mission to provide you the highest quality paper, the best possible service at the lowest possible prices.
迈克尔·斯科特造纸公司的使命是以最低的价格为您提供最高质量的纸张和最好的服务。

407
00:17:58.930 --> 00:17:59.650
Sounds good.
听起来不错。

408
00:17:59.970 --> 00:18:00.690
Just wait.
等着瞧吧。

409
00:18:00.930 --> 00:18:01.690
There's more.
还有呢。

410
00:18:01.930 --> 00:18:05.810
This paper business is more than just paper, more than just a business.
这造纸生意不仅仅是关于纸张，不仅仅是一笔生意。

411
00:18:06.110 --> 00:18:10.290
It's about establishing quality human relationships with our clients.
这是关于与我们的客户建立优质的人际关系。

412
00:18:10.530 --> 00:18:17.490
While little Timmy wakes up in the middle of the night with whooping cough and you need someone to call, we'll be there.
当小蒂米在半夜醒来患了百日咳，你需要有人打电话时，我们会出现。

413
00:18:17.490 --> 00:18:21.990
When sweet Christine gets stood up by her prom date, we'll be there.
当可爱的克里斯蒂娜被舞会伴侣放鸽子时，我们会出现。

414
00:18:22.170 --> 00:18:30.390
When the dam breaks in your backyard and the only thing that can stop the flow of water from flooding your house is a ream of paper, we'll be there.
当你们后院的水坝决堤，唯一能阻止水流淹没你房子的东西是一令纸时，我们会出现。

415
00:18:30.750 --> 00:18:33.850
At the Michael Scott paper company, we'll always be there.
在迈克尔·斯科特造纸公司，我们永远都会出现。

416
00:18:33.970 --> 00:18:41.450
Through thick and thin and sickness and health till death or retirement do us part, we'll be there.
无论顺境逆境、生老病死，直到死亡或退休将我们分开，我们都会出现。

417
00:18:41.650 --> 00:18:46.010
For a while, it's just pretty standard.
有一会儿，它相当标准。

418
00:18:46.270 --> 00:18:47.010
Kind of boilerplate.
有点像样板文案。

419
00:18:47.010 --> 00:18:47.270
Yeah.
是的。

420
00:18:47.510 --> 00:18:47.690
Yeah.
是的。

421
00:18:48.030 --> 00:18:51.090
But I really like it when he says we're more than just a business.
但我真的很喜欢他说我们不仅仅是一笔生意的时候。

422
00:18:51.090 --> 00:18:54.630
We're about quality human relationships with our clients.
我们致力于与客户建立优质的人际关系。

423
00:18:54.630 --> 00:18:55.570
I'm like, oh.
我想，哦。

424
00:18:56.110 --> 00:19:01.270
And then it goes off into some very specific examples of when you might be there for me.
然后它就列举了一些非常具体的例子，说明你什么时候可能会为我出现。

425
00:19:02.010 --> 00:19:03.530
But in the end, I liked it.
但总的来说，我挺喜欢的。

426
00:19:04.190 --> 00:19:08.030
I think I was a little curious about what kind of backyard you have that has a dam.
我只是有点好奇你到底有个什么样的后院，里面居然有个水坝。

427
00:19:10.990 --> 00:19:12.270
Well, listen, we'll be there.
听着，我们会出现的。

428
00:19:13.630 --> 00:19:17.890
Fast fact number three, Ellie Kemper is our new receptioniSt.
趣味冷知识之三，埃莉·坎珀是我们的新前台。

429
00:19:17.990 --> 00:19:18.390
Woo-hoo!
呜呼！

430
00:19:18.850 --> 00:19:20.350
We love Ellie.
我们爱埃莉。

431
00:19:20.670 --> 00:19:22.550
We are definitely going to have her on the show.
我们绝对要邀请她上节目。

432
00:19:23.190 --> 00:19:25.110
You know, Ellie and I both grew up in St. Louis.
你知道的，埃莉和我都是在圣路易斯长大的。

433
00:19:25.110 --> 00:19:26.310
Yes, I know.
是的，我知道。

434
00:19:26.550 --> 00:19:28.250
Now, I did not know her growing up.
不过，我从小并不认识她。

435
00:19:28.310 --> 00:19:30.070
She is six years younger than me.
她比我小六岁。

436
00:19:30.470 --> 00:19:36.870
I had actually graduated college and moved to Los Angeles while she was still in high school.
事实上，当我大学毕业搬到洛杉矶时，她还在读高中。

437
00:19:37.330 --> 00:19:43.690
I'm six years older than my husband, so you just described our relationship, I guess, had
我比我丈夫大六岁，所以我想这就描述了我们的关系，如果

438
00:19:43.690 --> 00:19:44.950
we known each other back then.
我们那时候就认识的话。

439
00:19:45.730 --> 00:19:49.690
By the way, do you know who her high school drama teacher was?
顺便问一下，你知道她的高中戏剧老师是谁吗？

440
00:19:50.530 --> 00:19:51.010
Ellie's?
埃莉的？

441
00:19:51.150 --> 00:19:51.490
Uh-huh.
嗯哼。

442
00:19:51.750 --> 00:19:51.970
No.
不知道。

443
00:19:52.690 --> 00:19:53.150
John Hamm.
乔恩·哈姆。

444
00:19:53.810 --> 00:19:55.050
Shut the front door!
开什么玩笑！

445
00:19:55.230 --> 00:19:55.370
Yeah.
是的。

446
00:19:55.770 --> 00:19:57.610
John Hamm also grew up in St. Louis.
乔恩·哈姆也是在圣路易斯长大的。

447
00:19:57.870 --> 00:20:02.590
I also did not know John Hamm growing up, even though we were closer in age.
我从小也不认识乔恩·哈姆，尽管我们年龄更接近。

448
00:20:02.770 --> 00:20:06.590
I can't believe that was Ellie's drama teacher.
我真不敢相信那是埃莉的戏剧老师。

449
00:20:06.790 --> 00:20:06.950
Yeah.
是的。

450
00:20:07.810 --> 00:20:10.930
But, of course, you know, Phyllis was also from St. Louis.
但当然，你知道的，菲利斯也是来自圣路易斯。

451
00:20:11.170 --> 00:20:11.370
Yes.
是的。

452
00:20:11.550 --> 00:20:13.450
Our director, Ken Kwapis, was from St. Louis.
我们的导演肯·夸皮斯来自圣路易斯。

453
00:20:13.670 --> 00:20:16.290
And our first AD, Rusty Mahmood, was from St. Louis.
我们的第一副导演拉斯蒂·马穆德也来自圣路易斯。

454
00:20:16.830 --> 00:20:18.290
So, we were all very excited.
所以，我们当时都非常兴奋。

455
00:20:18.710 --> 00:20:21.690
Well, you know, on the DVD commentary, there was a little bit of chatter.
嗯，你知道的，在DVD评论音轨里，大家聊了一点。

456
00:20:21.910 --> 00:20:25.010
On the DVD was Jenna, Jean, and Lee, and Justin.
参与DVD录制的有珍娜、珍、李和贾斯廷。

457
00:20:25.650 --> 00:20:25.830
Hmm.
嗯。

458
00:20:25.990 --> 00:20:26.490
Nice group.
很棒的组合。

459
00:20:26.650 --> 00:20:27.230
Nice group.
很棒的组合。

460
00:20:27.590 --> 00:20:31.850
There was a little bit of chatter about which city in America was most represented
大家聊到美国哪座城市在

461
00:20:31.850 --> 00:20:34.030
in the cast and crew of The Office.
《办公室》的演职人员中代表性最高。

462
00:20:34.030 --> 00:20:37.110
I think with the addition of Ellie, it became St. Louis.
我觉得随着埃莉的加入，变成了圣路易斯。

463
00:20:37.430 --> 00:20:38.330
It was Boston.
是波士顿。

464
00:20:38.750 --> 00:20:40.050
It became St. Louis.
后来变成了圣路易斯。

465
00:20:40.370 --> 00:20:40.730
Yes!
没错！

466
00:20:41.130 --> 00:20:46.970
And, Jenna, I want you to know, you have clearly been a—this is going to make me laugh—obsessed
而且，珍娜，我想让你知道，你显然一直是一个——这快把我逗笑了——对

467
00:20:46.970 --> 00:20:49.330
with facts for a long time.
各种冷知识痴迷了很久。

468
00:20:49.810 --> 00:20:53.790
I want you to hear what you brought to the DVD commentary.
