Her name was Mary.
她的名字叫玛丽。

926
00:41:59.220 --> 00:41:59.780
Mary?
玛丽？

927
00:41:59.780 --> 00:41:59.900
Mary.
玛丽。

928
00:42:00.320 --> 00:42:00.700
Yeah.
是啊。

929
00:42:00.940 --> 00:42:04.060
And this scene was not a thing where they have the same name.
这场戏原本也不是关于她们同名的情节。

930
00:42:04.200 --> 00:42:05.300
That was a late addition.
那是后来才加上去的。

931
00:42:05.820 --> 00:42:06.800
Oh, wow.
哦，哇。

932
00:42:06.800 --> 00:42:08.400
I love this scene.
我喜欢这场戏。

933
00:42:08.560 --> 00:42:08.960
I know.
我知道。

934
00:42:09.060 --> 00:42:09.420
Me too.
我也是。

935
00:42:10.360 --> 00:42:13.180
Well, fan question from Kelly Ann M.
好，来自凯利·安·M的粉丝提问。

936
00:42:13.420 --> 00:42:17.620
Who says, we need to track Erin's hair progression.
她说，我们需要追踪艾琳的发型变化过程。

937
00:42:18.120 --> 00:42:19.700
When did she go red?
她是什么时候变成红发女郎的？

938
00:42:20.320 --> 00:42:23.400
She will eventually win cutest redhead in the office.
她最终会赢得办公室最可爱红发女郎的称号。

939
00:42:23.600 --> 00:42:25.120
But she's a brunette here.
但她在这里是个深发色。

940
00:42:25.280 --> 00:42:26.360
We need to track it.
我们需要追踪一下。

941
00:42:27.320 --> 00:42:29.580
But, well, Lee Eisenberg filled me in on this.
但是，好吧，李·艾森伯格把这事儿透漏给我了。

942
00:42:29.800 --> 00:42:31.400
Well, I remember some of this.
好吧，我记得其中一些。

943
00:42:31.840 --> 00:42:38.820
He said when Ellie showed up for her very first day of work, her hair color was almost identical to mine.
他说，当艾莉第一天去上班时，她的发色和我几乎一模一样。

944
00:42:39.020 --> 00:42:39.160
Yep.
没错。

945
00:42:39.160 --> 00:42:41.680
And everyone freaked out.
然后所有人都吓坏了。

946
00:42:42.080 --> 00:42:42.340
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

947
00:42:42.500 --> 00:42:51.480
They were not trying to tell a story that Pam was being replaced by a sort of lookalike person.
他们可不是想讲一个帕姆被某种长相相似的人取代的故事。

948
00:42:51.780 --> 00:42:59.980
And they were really worried that if they put her on camera having the same color hair, that it was going to tell a story they weren't telling.
他们真的很担心，如果让顶着同样发色的她出镜，就会传达出他们并不想讲的故事。

949
00:43:00.400 --> 00:43:00.540
Yeah.
是啊。

950
00:43:01.100 --> 00:43:07.460
So they had to change the whole schedule for the day and color her hair.
所以他们不得不改变当天的整个行程，去把她的头发染色。

951
00:43:07.800 --> 00:43:12.240
I was in the hair and makeup trailer when she was getting her hair colored by Kim Ferry.
当时她正在发型和化妆车里让金·费里染发。

952
00:43:12.520 --> 00:43:15.880
And I guess Kim just has a drawer of hair color.
我猜金正好有一个装染发剂的抽屉。

953
00:43:16.080 --> 00:43:16.600
Sure.
没错。

954
00:43:16.600 --> 00:43:21.120
And they came up with this sort of brunette color, which will now evolve.
然后他们想出了这种深褐色，接下来它会发生变化。

955
00:43:21.460 --> 00:43:27.240
The character of Erin was also not originally meant to become a full-time regular character.
艾琳这个角色最初也不是注定要成为常规全职角色的。

956
00:43:27.420 --> 00:43:29.640
This was just going to be a few episodes.
这本来只打算拍几集。

957
00:43:29.980 --> 00:43:31.900
So we will track it.
所以我们会关注这一点。

958
00:43:32.020 --> 00:43:40.100
But I believe her hair is going to get to sort of change over to that red color as they make her a more permanent character on the show.
但我相信随着她成为剧中更长驻的角色，她的头发会慢慢变成那种红色。

959
00:43:40.560 --> 00:43:42.340
Yeah, I remember that day.
对，我记得那天。

960
00:43:42.560 --> 00:43:44.840
And Ellie is such a team player, you know?
艾莉真是个很有团队精神的人，你知道吗？

961
00:43:45.200 --> 00:43:46.740
And my memory's correct.
如果我的记忆没出错的话。

962
00:43:46.740 --> 00:43:49.320
They died at one time and then died it again.
他们染了一次，然后又染了一次。

963
00:43:49.560 --> 00:43:50.100
Oh, boy.
天哪。

964
00:43:50.380 --> 00:43:50.600
Yeah.
对。

965
00:43:51.040 --> 00:43:51.740
Oh, boy.
天哪。

966
00:43:52.640 --> 00:43:56.320
Michael Scott Paper Company has kind of come already to a standstill.
迈克尔·斯科特纸业公司已经有点陷入停顿了。

967
00:43:56.880 --> 00:43:57.980
They don't know what to do.
他们不知道该怎么办。

968
00:43:58.120 --> 00:43:59.000
They're like, what do we do now?
他们就像是在说，我们现在该干嘛？

969
00:43:59.160 --> 00:44:00.920
They're just sitting there looking at each other.
他们就坐在那里大眼瞪小眼。

970
00:44:01.240 --> 00:44:05.460
Yeah, Michael's working on his Evite for his pancake luncheon.
对，迈克尔正在为他的煎饼午餐会制作电子请柬。

971
00:44:05.460 --> 00:44:07.860
We had a fan catch from Ria V.
我们收到了粉丝里亚·V.和阿比·M.的发现，

972
00:44:08.120 --> 00:44:14.120
and Abby M., who noticed if you look closely, it says that the luncheon is going to take place on Saturday.
他们注意到如果仔细看，上面写着午餐会将在星期六举行。

973
00:44:14.440 --> 00:44:15.580
I saw that, too.
我也看到了。

974
00:44:16.240 --> 00:44:21.860
Also, during this scene, you can hear the sounds of toilets flushing through the pipes overhead.
另外，在这场戏中，你能听到头顶管道里传来冲马桶的声音。

975
00:44:21.960 --> 00:44:24.200
You're really getting a sense of this workspace.
你真的能感受到这个工作场所的氛围。

976
00:44:24.760 --> 00:44:32.100
So we could actually hear toilets flushing if somebody used the real bathrooms outside.
所以如果外面有人使用真正的洗手间，我们其实能听到冲水声。

977
00:44:34.100 --> 00:44:37.080
So while we were shooting, they would not allow anyone in there.
所以在我们拍摄时，他们不允许任何人进去。

978
00:44:37.200 --> 00:44:41.820
But while we rehearsed or while we were waiting to shoot, people could use the bathrooMs.
但当我们排练或等待拍摄时，人们可以使用洗手间。

979
00:44:41.820 --> 00:44:45.580
And so we would really sit in that room and hear flushing toilets.
所以我们真的会坐在那个房间里听到冲马桶的声音。

980
00:44:48.020 --> 00:44:52.840
And I also don't know if you noticed the spots that BJ and I are sitting in.
我也不知道你们有没有注意到我和BJ坐的位置。

981
00:44:52.840 --> 00:45:02.480
And when we first walked into that room, our natural inclination was to sit across from one another at the table because it gave you maximum space for your elbows.
当我们第一次走进那个房间时，我们的本能倾向是坐在桌子对面，因为这样能给你的手肘留出最大的空间。

982
00:45:02.940 --> 00:45:03.120
Sure, sure.
确实，确实。

983
00:45:03.340 --> 00:45:06.420
You know, but you couldn't shoot us that way.
你知道的，但那样就没法拍我们了。

984
00:45:06.640 --> 00:45:18.420
We had to both sort of sit with our backs like scrunched up against that wall kind of next to each other facing Michael because it was literally the only way to get us on camera.
我们俩必须靠在墙上，背部蜷缩着，挨得很近，面向迈克尔，因为字面意思，这是唯一能把我们拍进镜头的方法。

985
00:45:18.920 --> 00:45:28.880
Last week in Dream Team for the DVD commentary for that episode, Matt Sohn actually talked about this episode and how hard it was to shoot in that room because of the angles.
上周在讲到那一集的DVD评论音轨时，马特·松确实谈到了这一集以及在那个房间里因为角度问题有多难拍。

986
00:45:29.120 --> 00:45:30.320
Exactly what you were talking about.
完全和你说的一样。

987
00:45:30.440 --> 00:45:31.920
They kept catching each other.
他们总是不小心拍到对方。

988
00:45:32.160 --> 00:45:34.900
Our two camera operators kept catching each other in the shot.
我们的两个摄像师在镜头里总是不小心拍到对方。

989
00:45:35.320 --> 00:45:39.380
So they had to sort of position you guys so that they could get these single camera shots of you.
所以他们必须调整你们的位置，这样才能拍到你们的单人镜头。

990
00:45:39.660 --> 00:45:44.520
Yeah, I think that's something you don't think about when you watch the scene is how there's all these extra people in the room.
对，我想看这场戏时你不会想到的是，房间里居然有这么多多余的人。

991
00:45:44.640 --> 00:45:44.900
Yeah.
对。

992
00:45:45.100 --> 00:45:47.900
But they're magically avoiding one another on camera.
但他们在镜头前神奇地避开了彼此。

993
00:45:48.420 --> 00:45:54.720
But at the same time, Steve as Michael can't walk from his desk to the poker table without bonking his leg into things.
但与此同时，饰演迈克尔的史蒂夫从他的办公桌走到扑克桌时，却免不了让腿磕到各种东西。

994
00:45:54.820 --> 00:45:56.000
You know, it's like that tight.
你知道的，就是那么挤。

995
00:45:56.260 --> 00:46:02.300
Well, now Michael is going to ask Pam to make 800 copies of his unparalleled customer service coupon.
好吧，现在迈克尔要让帕姆复印800份他那无与伦比的客服优惠券。

996
00:46:02.640 --> 00:46:05.500
But Pam has a talking head, and I really relate to this.
但帕姆有一段内心独白，我对此深有同感。

997
00:46:06.020 --> 00:46:12.760
She says, if I make this one copy, then I'll become the girl who makes copies, and then I'm basically a receptionist again.
她说，如果我复印了这一份，那我就会变成那个专门复印的女孩，然后我基本上又成了前台接待员了。

998
00:46:13.260 --> 00:46:18.380
And I don't know if you noticed where the phone was on that table, but it is right in front of Pam.
我不知道你们有没有注意到那张桌子上的电话在哪里，它就在帕姆的正前方。

999
00:46:18.640 --> 00:46:21.860
So she's already clearly closest to the phone.
所以她显然离电话最近。

1000
00:46:21.860 --> 00:46:25.500
And even later when it rings, Michael says, answer it.
甚至后来电话响的时候，迈克尔还说，接电话。

1001
00:46:26.020 --> 00:46:26.560
I know.
我知道。

1002
00:46:26.760 --> 00:46:26.840
Right?
对吧？

1003
00:46:27.100 --> 00:46:27.320
Yeah.
是啊。

1004
00:46:27.840 --> 00:46:34.140
She's really trying to break out of this role of receptionist, and she refuses to make the copy.
她真的想摆脱前台这个角色，而且她拒绝复印文件。

1005
00:46:34.380 --> 00:46:36.460
She doesn't want to go down Putnam Road, guys.
她不想走帕特南路，伙计们。

1006
00:46:36.680 --> 00:46:37.280
She doesn't.
她真的不想。

1007
00:46:37.400 --> 00:46:39.760
She wants the other path, the more exciting path.
她想要另一条路，那条更刺激的路。

1008
00:46:40.260 --> 00:46:43.440
Well, it's a pretty big day for a few other characters at Dunder Mifflin.
话说回来，对于邓德米弗林的另外几个角色来说，这也是相当重要的一天。

1009
00:46:44.000 --> 00:46:46.580
Dwight is going to take Andy hunting.
德怀特要带安迪去打猎。

1010
00:46:47.640 --> 00:46:49.180
They're like buddy-buddy.
他们就像哥们儿一样。

1011
00:46:49.180 --> 00:46:55.000
There is so much more of this scene where they're sort of wrestling and like doing all this stuff.
这场戏里还有很多他们互相摔跤和做各种动作的内容。

1012
00:46:55.380 --> 00:46:56.920
It goes on for so long.
持续了非常久。

1013
00:46:57.080 --> 00:46:57.860
I have no doubt.
我毫不怀疑。

1014
00:46:58.060 --> 00:47:06.440
Do not ask the fellas to roughhouse or wrestle in a scene unless you want to have an hour of additional footage of it.
千万别让这几个家伙在戏里打闹或摔跤，除非你想多出一个小时的素材。

1015
00:47:06.560 --> 00:47:15.960
Because anytime they had Rainn Wilson and John Krasinski have to do something like that, like last week's knock-knock joke thing, any scuffle.
因为每次让雷恩·威尔逊和约翰·卡拉辛斯基拍这种戏，比如上周那个敲门笑话的桥段，任何推搡。

1016
00:47:15.960 --> 00:47:25.180
It's worth a watch in the deleted scenes because those two fellas, they go for so long in all their fake different ways of attacking each other.
在删减片段里绝对值得一看，因为那两个家伙在用各种假装袭击对方的方式时，真的持续了太久。

1017
00:47:25.260 --> 00:47:28.140
And they get so into John's personal space.
而且他们离约翰的个人空间太近了。

1018
00:47:28.720 --> 00:47:30.540
And his face is hilarious.
他的表情太搞笑勒。

1019
00:47:30.740 --> 00:47:32.120
I don't know how he kept a straight face.
我不知道他是怎么忍住不笑的。

1020
00:47:33.000 --> 00:47:37.040
Andy had a talking head that was deleted where he talks about this bromance.
安迪原本有一段被删掉的单人访谈，他在里面谈到了这段兄弟情。

1021
00:47:37.160 --> 00:47:38.900
You know, we see Dwight's in the episode.
你知道的，我们在这一集里看到了德怀特的情形。

1022
00:47:38.900 --> 00:47:42.220
But Andy had a counterpart one, and I think we need to hear it.
但安迪有一个对应的单人访谈，我觉得我们得听听。

1023
00:47:42.440 --> 00:47:42.600
Oh.
哦。

1024
00:47:43.560 --> 00:47:44.520
Let me tell you something.
我跟你说个事。

1025
00:47:44.760 --> 00:47:49.500
When Angela and I split, I went through it big time.
我和安吉拉分手后，我真的经历了一段非常痛苦的时期。

1026
00:47:49.960 --> 00:47:51.100
Lost my high notes.
高音都唱不上去了。

1027
00:47:51.680 --> 00:47:53.760
Top of my range was like, boo.
我的音域上限就像是，呜。

1028
00:47:56.220 --> 00:47:57.240
Then it took some time.
后来花了一些时间。

1029
00:47:57.700 --> 00:47:58.980
I got my heel on.
我振作起来了。

1030
00:47:59.320 --> 00:48:00.920
I got some perspective on.
我调整好了心态。

1031
00:48:01.620 --> 00:48:06.160
And I found a new friend in the most unlikely of places.
我在最意想不到的地方找到了一个新朋友。

1032
00:48:06.980 --> 00:48:08.160
The enemy bin.
敌人的阵营。

1033
00:48:10.240 --> 00:48:11.360
And now...
现在……

1034
00:48:11.360 --> 00:48:11.820
Oh.
哦。

1035
00:48:23.180 --> 00:48:24.380
He got his high notes back.
他的高音找回来了。

1036
00:48:24.480 --> 00:48:25.020
He did.
是的。

1037
00:48:25.340 --> 00:48:26.320
He got his heel on.
他振作起来了。

1038
00:48:26.380 --> 00:48:27.760
He got his perspective on.
他调整好心态了。

1039
00:48:27.900 --> 00:48:29.460
And he found it all in the enemy bin.
这一切都是在敌人的阵营里找到的。

1040
00:48:29.600 --> 00:48:30.080
I know.
我知道。

1041
00:48:30.900 --> 00:48:35.360
I also really love the storyline of Charles asking Jim for the rundown.
我也很喜欢查尔斯让吉姆交出一份工作总结的剧情。

1042
00:48:35.580 --> 00:48:36.100
Yes.
对。

1043
00:48:36.320 --> 00:48:39.720
And Jim has no idea what a rundown is.
而吉姆根本不知道什么是工作总结。

1044
00:48:39.720 --> 00:48:41.940
And he's not going to ask.
而且他也不打算问。

1045
00:48:42.500 --> 00:48:43.620
He's too afraid.
他太害怕了。

1046
00:48:43.920 --> 00:48:44.360
I know.
我知道。

1047
00:48:44.680 --> 00:48:49.800
So when we reached out to Gene and Lee, they said that this whole rundown story was a late
所以当我们联系吉恩和李时，他们说这个工作总结的故事是一个临时的

1048
00:48:49.800 --> 00:48:50.200
addition.
补充。

1049
00:48:50.740 --> 00:48:52.580
It was part of a rewrite session.
它是重写剧本环节的一部分。

1050
00:48:52.580 --> 00:48:55.620
And you know, we've talked about how some of the writers would break off into these little
你知道的，我们之前聊过编剧们有时会分成这样的小组

1051
00:48:55.620 --> 00:48:56.040
pods.
播客。

1052
00:48:56.720 --> 00:49:01.640
So Paul Lieberstein, Jen Salata, and BJ Novak broke away from the group.
所以保罗·利伯斯坦、珍·萨拉塔和B·J·诺瓦克脱离了大家。

1053
00:49:01.840 --> 00:49:05.820
And in about two hours, they came up with this whole rundown storyline.
大约两小时后，他们就想出了整个工作汇报的故事线。

1054
00:49:06.080 --> 00:49:07.080
I love it.
我太喜欢了。

1055
00:49:07.260 --> 00:49:07.920
I know.
我知道。

1056
00:49:07.920 --> 00:49:11.780
And then Justin Spitzer said, they thought this was great.
然后贾斯廷·斯皮策说，他们觉得这个主意太棒了。

1057
00:49:11.900 --> 00:49:13.860
This sort of rundown was sort of this vague term.
这种“工作汇报”其实是个挺模糊的词。

1058
00:49:14.040 --> 00:49:16.440
And no one in the writer's room really knew what it meant.
编剧室里没人真正知道它是什么意思。

1059
00:49:16.560 --> 00:49:17.520
So they thought, well, that's perfect.
所以他们想，嗯，这太完美了。

1060
00:49:17.660 --> 00:49:18.840
Maybe Jim wouldn't know either.
也许吉姆也不知道。

1061
00:49:19.160 --> 00:49:24.000
And they said after the episode aired that they got mail that people were like, yeah,
他们说剧集播出后，收到了观众的信，大家都在说，对啊，

1062
00:49:24.120 --> 00:49:24.900
duh, a rundown.
废话，就是汇报。

1063
00:49:25.120 --> 00:49:25.900
Yeah, rundown.
对啊，工作汇报。

1064
00:49:26.040 --> 00:49:27.400
Like people had heard of it.
好像大家都听说过似的。

1065
00:49:27.480 --> 00:49:28.700
And they were like, no way.
他们就想，开什么玩笑。

1066
00:49:28.940 --> 00:49:30.480
So I looked it up.
于是我查了一下。

1067
00:49:30.660 --> 00:49:32.980
I Googled because we're ladies that Google.
我用谷歌搜了，因为我们是会用谷歌搜的时代女性。

1068
00:49:33.200 --> 00:49:33.480
We are.
我们确实是。

1069
00:49:33.480 --> 00:49:35.760
I just wrote, what is a rundown?
我当时就输入了，什么是工作汇报？

1070
00:49:36.240 --> 00:49:38.440
And this is what the internet had to say.
这就是互联网的解释。

1071
00:49:39.320 --> 00:49:42.980
In businesses, a rundown is a status report or summary.
在商业领域，工作汇报就是状态报告或总结。

1072
00:49:43.680 --> 00:49:44.040
Yeah.
对。

1073
00:49:44.280 --> 00:49:47.660
I mean, common sense would lead me in that direction.
我的意思是，常识也会引导我往这个方向想。

1074
00:49:47.660 --> 00:49:53.600
If I had to guess, I would think, oh, I should make a list of all my current clients and their
如果让我猜，我会觉得，哦，我应该列一份我所有的现有客户名单以及他们的

1075
00:49:53.600 --> 00:49:54.000
status.
状态。

1076
00:49:54.000 --> 00:49:56.640
