01:11:03.720 --> 01:11:06.100
I love that Michael's like, stop with the texting machine.
我太喜欢迈克尔那种“别玩那个发短信的机器了”的腔调了。

1528
01:11:08.660 --> 01:11:14.040
So here we are, Jenna, at our second pair of sunglasses at 14 minutes, 59 seconds.
所以我们现在到了这里，珍娜，在14分59秒时戴上了我们的第二副太阳镜。

1529
01:11:14.260 --> 01:11:14.840
Oh, yes.
哦，是的。

1530
01:11:14.980 --> 01:11:16.520
I have the same time code.
我的时间码也是一样的。

1531
01:11:16.860 --> 01:11:19.300
What do you want to say about these sunglasses?
关于这副太阳镜，你想说点什么？

1532
01:11:19.700 --> 01:11:21.460
Wait, can we say it right at the same time?
等等，我们能同时说吗？

1533
01:11:21.500 --> 01:11:23.840
It'll be jarbled, but let's see if it sounds the same.
声音会混在一起，但看看听起来是不是一样。

1534
01:11:23.940 --> 01:11:24.220
Okay.
好。

1535
01:11:24.220 --> 01:11:36.660
These sunglasses were inspired by Joaquin Phoenix's appearance on The David Letterman Show in 2009 when he was promoting I'm Still Here.
这副太阳镜的灵感来源于杰昆·菲尼克斯在2009年大卫·莱特曼秀上的亮相，当时他正在宣传《我仍在这里》。

1536
01:11:36.920 --> 01:11:38.580
It was a very odd appearance.
那是一次非常奇怪的亮相。

1537
01:11:38.580 --> 01:11:40.340
I watched that in real time.
我当时实时观看了那期节目。

1538
01:11:40.340 --> 01:11:43.980
But it was all part of like a marketing ploy or something.
但这一切其实都是某种营销伎俩之类的一部分。

1539
01:11:44.220 --> 01:11:52.420
He did this film, and I guess he was trying to make us believe that he had actually switched careers.
他拍了这部电影，我猜他是想让我们相信他真的转行了。

1540
01:11:52.760 --> 01:11:56.220
And it was sort of like an Andy Kaufman-esque thing.
这有点像安迪·考夫曼式的风格。

1541
01:11:56.220 --> 01:11:57.960
I took a screen grab.
我截了一张图。

1542
01:11:58.320 --> 01:12:01.600
I did a side-by-side for you, lady.
我为你做了一张对比图，女士。

1543
01:12:01.900 --> 01:12:03.140
Oh, give it to me.
哦，快给我看看。

1544
01:12:03.300 --> 01:12:06.440
Joaquin Phoenix and Ryan, same sunglasses.
杰昆·菲尼克斯和瑞安，戴着同款太阳镜。

1545
01:12:06.900 --> 01:12:07.960
Putting that in stories.
把它发到动态里。

1546
01:12:08.240 --> 01:12:10.180
They retail for about $400.
它们的零售价大约是400美元。

1547
01:12:10.780 --> 01:12:11.160
What?
什么？

1548
01:12:11.460 --> 01:12:12.100
Very expensive.
太贵了。

1549
01:12:12.920 --> 01:12:13.160
Yeah.
是啊。

1550
01:12:13.580 --> 01:12:14.500
Are you crazy?
你疯了吗？

1551
01:12:14.640 --> 01:12:15.380
Are they prescription?
是处方镜吗？

1552
01:12:15.880 --> 01:12:17.200
No, they're just fancy.
不是，只是普通的时尚墨镜。

1553
01:12:17.340 --> 01:12:17.960
That's nuts.
太疯狂了。

1554
01:12:18.360 --> 01:12:25.360
I mean, if I bought that pair of sunglasses, I might as well just flush $400 down the toilet because I'm going to lose them in less than a year.
我是说，如果我买那副墨镜，还不如直接把400美元冲进马桶，因为我不到一年就会弄丢。

1555
01:12:26.220 --> 01:12:27.520
Some people like fancy sunglasses.
有些人就喜欢高级墨镜。

1556
01:12:27.760 --> 01:12:29.020
And listen, you do you.
听着，你开心就好。

1557
01:12:29.340 --> 01:12:30.180
But I don't know.
但我不知道。

1558
01:12:30.380 --> 01:12:32.640
Three kids, sunglasses, soccer games.
三个孩子，墨镜，足球比赛。

1559
01:12:32.820 --> 01:12:34.160
Mine just get wrecked.
我的墨镜转眼就毁了。

1560
01:12:34.540 --> 01:12:39.520
I splurged on a pair of $200 prescription sunglasses.
我曾经奢侈了一把，买了一副200美元的处方墨镜。

1561
01:12:39.520 --> 01:12:41.360
I have to have prescription sunglasses.
我必须戴处方墨镜。

1562
01:12:41.620 --> 01:12:49.180
Because I was doing the double glasses for so long, you know, where you buy a giant pair of regular sunglasses that you put over your real glasses.
因为我戴双层眼镜太久了，你知道的，就是买那种超大的普通墨镜，套在你的真眼镜外面。

1563
01:12:49.480 --> 01:12:49.920
I saw it, Jenna.
我看到了，珍娜。

1564
01:12:50.020 --> 01:12:52.780
You look like you need to live in like a Florida retirement community.
你看起来就像该去佛罗里达州退休社区住一样。

1565
01:12:53.220 --> 01:12:53.340
I know.
我知道。

1566
01:12:53.520 --> 01:12:54.440
And you know what?
你知道吗？

1567
01:12:54.440 --> 01:12:59.280
I managed to keep those prescription sunglasses for almost two years.
我居然把那副处方墨镜保留了将近两年。

1568
01:13:00.360 --> 01:13:02.200
I lost them somewhere.
后来不知道在哪里弄丢了。

1569
01:13:02.300 --> 01:13:04.300
And now I'm back to double glasses.
现在我又得戴双层眼镜了。

1570
01:13:05.040 --> 01:13:06.240
You know what we need?
你知道我们需要什么吗？

1571
01:13:06.420 --> 01:13:06.720
What?
什么？

1572
01:13:07.000 --> 01:13:09.680
Josh says I need the chain on my glasses.
乔什说我的眼镜需要配根挂绳。

1573
01:13:10.320 --> 01:13:12.020
Oh, I have a story about my mom.
哦，我有个关于我妈的故事。

1574
01:13:12.180 --> 01:13:12.880
What happens?
怎么了？

1575
01:13:12.980 --> 01:13:13.680
That's it, right?
就是这样，对吧？

1576
01:13:13.780 --> 01:13:14.220
That's it.
就是这样。

1577
01:13:14.320 --> 01:13:15.540
Your sexy days are over.
你性感日子到头了。

1578
01:13:15.680 --> 01:13:17.760
If you put your glasses on a chain, I don't know.
如果你给眼镜配上挂绳，我可说不准了。

1579
01:13:17.760 --> 01:13:21.040
Well, my mom, we affectionately call her Lucy.
我妈嘛，我们亲切地叫她露西。

1580
01:13:21.640 --> 01:13:26.760
Because when you go into a store with her, it's like you're shopping with Lucille Ball from I Love Lucy.
因为你跟她一起逛商店，就像在和《我爱露西》里的露西尔·鲍尔一起购物一样。

1581
01:13:26.760 --> 01:13:33.800
Because she will manage to get tangled in or knock over any store display.
因为她总能把自己缠进店里的任何货架，或者把它们撞倒。

1582
01:13:34.160 --> 01:13:37.700
I was going to say, does she knock things over or try to put too many chocolates in her mouth?
我本来想说，她是把东西撞倒，还是试图往嘴里塞太多巧克力？

1583
01:13:37.700 --> 01:13:44.760
So, we were shopping with her and she had on her glasses around one of those chains.
当时我们跟她一起逛街，她的眼镜挂在一根那样的链子上。

1584
01:13:45.200 --> 01:13:48.140
But it was winter, so she also had a scarf.
但那是冬天，所以她还系着围巾。

1585
01:13:48.520 --> 01:13:54.280
And she also had, I don't know why, like long necklaces, a purse, you know, cross-bodied.
而且她还戴着——不知道为什么——长项链，还有一个斜挎包。

1586
01:13:54.280 --> 01:13:58.860
And she goes to take off her cross-body purse.
然后她去取下斜挎包。

1587
01:13:59.100 --> 01:14:01.680
It yanks on her sunglasses chain.
包带扯到了她的眼镜链。

1588
01:14:02.020 --> 01:14:03.320
Elbows are flying.
胳膊肘乱挥。

1589
01:14:03.520 --> 01:14:06.300
She takes down a whole display of earrings.
她撞倒了一整架耳环。

1590
01:14:06.680 --> 01:14:07.140
Oh, no.
不会吧。

1591
01:14:07.380 --> 01:14:11.800
My sister and I are like rushing in to like help her.
我和姐姐赶紧冲过去帮忙。

1592
01:14:11.900 --> 01:14:12.700
She's tangled.
她缠成了一团。

1593
01:14:12.960 --> 01:14:15.140
She looks like a cat tangled in string.
她看起来就像一只缠在毛线里的猫。

1594
01:14:15.740 --> 01:14:18.500
And just displays are falling down.
货架哗啦啦地往下掉。

1595
01:14:19.120 --> 01:14:25.540
So, whenever I think about putting my glasses on a chain, that memory comes back to me.
所以，每当我想给眼镜配挂绳时，那个记忆就会浮现出来。

1596
01:14:25.680 --> 01:14:27.280
And I think, that could be me.
然后我想，那可能会是我。

1597
01:14:27.740 --> 01:14:28.800
I could be that.
我也可能会那样。

1598
01:14:28.980 --> 01:14:30.500
I could easily have done that.
我完全有可能做出那种事。

1599
01:14:30.780 --> 01:14:31.960
I could take down a display.
我也可能撞翻货架。

1600
01:14:32.280 --> 01:14:33.800
You could take down a display.
你确实可能撞翻货架。

1601
01:14:34.080 --> 01:14:37.560
I saw you almost take out a few people on an airplane with a guitar.
我看到你差点在飞机上用一把吉他砸到几个人。

1602
01:14:38.100 --> 01:14:38.440
Yeah.
对。

1603
01:14:38.760 --> 01:14:39.060
Yeah.
没错。

1604
01:14:39.480 --> 01:14:43.760
I mean, so I can't chain my glasses is the bottom line.
我的意思是，所以说我不能给眼镜配链子，这就是底线。

1605
01:14:43.840 --> 01:14:44.300
Oh, well.
噢，好吧。

1606
01:14:44.960 --> 01:14:45.540
I'm sorry.
对不起。

1607
01:14:45.780 --> 01:14:46.020
Okay.
好吧。

1608
01:14:46.020 --> 01:14:54.100
But we spent $400 on these glasses for the character of Ryan for this very subtle inside
但我们为了瑞恩这个角色花了400美元买这副眼镜，是为了这样一个非常微妙的内行

1609
01:14:54.100 --> 01:14:58.280
joke that clearly Ryan is a Joaquin Phoenix fan and probably saw that.
笑话：显然瑞恩是华金·菲尼克斯的粉丝，可能看过那部电影。

1610
01:14:58.300 --> 01:14:59.400
It's in character.
这很符合角色设定。

1611
01:14:59.720 --> 01:15:02.940
He is the kind of guy who has to have the thing, the latest thing.
他就是那种必须拥有最新玩意儿的人。

1612
01:15:03.360 --> 01:15:06.080
Even though his mom is driving him to work.
尽管他妈还开车送他去上班。

1613
01:15:06.280 --> 01:15:06.660
Yes.
没错。

1614
01:15:06.900 --> 01:15:07.360
Exactly.
正是如此。

1615
01:15:07.780 --> 01:15:08.900
He's really not employed.
他其实没有工作。

1616
01:15:09.080 --> 01:15:10.320
Like, he's not earning a paycheck.
也就是说，他没有薪水可拿。

1617
01:15:10.480 --> 01:15:10.920
He isn't.
确实没有。

1618
01:15:10.940 --> 01:15:12.640
He's going to get $400 sunglasses.
但他却要买400美元的太阳镜。

1619
01:15:12.640 --> 01:15:19.280
At 15 minutes, 10 seconds, right as Pam is walking up, there's a great shot of some
在15分10秒的时候，就在帕姆走过来的那一刻，有一个非常棒的镜头，拍到了一些

1620
01:15:19.280 --> 01:15:20.700
fakie grocery bags.
假冒的杂货袋。

1621
01:15:20.980 --> 01:15:21.980
Ooh, fakie bags.
噢，假袋子。

1622
01:15:22.060 --> 01:15:23.400
We got some fakie bags.
我们有几个假袋子。

1623
01:15:23.720 --> 01:15:29.360
And Jenna, you shared on the commentary something that jogged my memory.
珍娜，你在评论音轨里分享的一些事勾起了我的回忆。

1624
01:15:29.900 --> 01:15:32.880
It took me back immediately to this day.
它瞬间把我带回了那一天。

1625
01:15:32.880 --> 01:15:38.400
Hey, you shared while you were filming this parking lot scene, the paparazzi snuck onto
嘿，你分享过在拍摄这个停车场场景时，狗仔队偷偷溜进了

1626
01:15:38.400 --> 01:15:38.900
our set.
我们的片场。

1627
01:15:39.420 --> 01:15:40.220
Oh my gosh.
噢天哪。

1628
01:15:40.220 --> 01:15:41.000
I remember that.
我记得那个。

1629
01:15:41.120 --> 01:15:41.580
Yes.
是的。

1630
01:15:41.680 --> 01:15:42.900
We had a guy.
我们当时有个家伙。

1631
01:15:43.240 --> 01:15:45.140
So, guys, we weren't on a big lot.
所以，伙计们，我们不在一个大型片场里。

1632
01:15:45.300 --> 01:15:46.200
We've shared that before.
我们以前分享过这个。

1633
01:15:46.700 --> 01:15:48.040
We didn't have security.
我们没有安保。

1634
01:15:48.040 --> 01:15:49.140
You just drove in.
你们直接就能把车开进来。

1635
01:15:49.280 --> 01:15:49.680
You did.
确实如此。

1636
01:15:50.440 --> 01:15:52.900
And after this day, we got a security guard.
而就在这一天之后，我们有了一个保安。

1637
01:15:53.020 --> 01:15:53.880
In a little hut.
在一个小亭子里。

1638
01:15:54.200 --> 01:15:54.400
Yeah.
对。

1639
01:15:54.560 --> 01:15:54.740
Yeah.
没错。

1640
01:15:55.060 --> 01:16:00.440
This paparazzi guy clearly staked us out, realized you could just drive right on the set, came
这个狗仔队家伙显然踩过点，发现你可以直接开车进片场，于是就

1641
01:16:00.440 --> 01:16:06.120
right on, and just started clicking pictures of the set, the parking lot, actors coming
直接闯了进来，开始疯狂拍摄片场、停车场以及走出

1642
01:16:06.120 --> 01:16:06.960
out of their trailers.
房车的演员们的照片。

1643
01:16:07.120 --> 01:16:09.040
They got one of Steve coming out of his trailer.
他们拍到了一张史蒂夫从他房车里出来的照片。

1644
01:16:09.240 --> 01:16:11.620
And it took us all a while to be like, oh, who's that guy?
我们花了很长时间才反应过来：噢，那家伙是谁？

1645
01:16:11.740 --> 01:16:12.220
Oh my God.
噢天哪。

1646
01:16:12.300 --> 01:16:12.660
Oh, wait, wait.
噢，等等，等等。

1647
01:16:12.760 --> 01:16:13.040
We don't.
我们不。

1648
01:16:13.140 --> 01:16:13.960
No one knows that guy.
没人认识那家伙。

1649
01:16:14.160 --> 01:16:17.540
Did I mention in the commentary why we think this happened?
我在评论音轨里提到过我们为什么觉得会发生这种事吗？

1650
01:16:17.540 --> 01:16:24.120
And finally, after five seasons, John had started dating Emily Blunt.
最后，在经历了五季之后，约翰开始和艾米莉·布朗特约会了。

1651
01:16:24.220 --> 01:16:24.820
Oh, no.
哦，不。

1652
01:16:25.480 --> 01:16:25.940
Yeah.
对。

1653
01:16:26.320 --> 01:16:30.360
So, that was sort of tabloidy interesting.
所以，那有点像八卦杂志那样有趣。

1654
01:16:30.700 --> 01:16:31.060
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1655
01:16:31.300 --> 01:16:36.440
Until now, none of us did anything of tabloid interest, basically.
在此之前，我们基本上没有人做过任何有八卦价值的事。

1656
01:16:36.780 --> 01:16:37.000
No.
没有。

1657
01:16:37.000 --> 01:16:40.280
So, I remember this because I was dating Lee at the time.
所以，我记得这件事，因为我当时在和李交往。

1658
01:16:40.440 --> 01:16:46.020
He and I were starting to get serious, and John started dating Emily, and we became couple
我和他开始变得认真起来，约翰开始和艾米丽交往，然后我们成了情侣

1659
01:16:46.020 --> 01:16:46.380
friends.
朋友。

1660
01:16:46.380 --> 01:16:46.880
You did.
你们确实是。

1661
01:16:47.000 --> 01:16:48.580
You guys would, like, go and do things.
你们俩会一起去参加各种活动。

1662
01:16:48.780 --> 01:16:49.200
We did.
我们确实去了。

1663
01:16:49.200 --> 01:16:54.080
And the news finally broke that the two of them were dating one another.
然后终于爆出他们俩在交往的新闻。

1664
01:16:54.240 --> 01:16:56.860
And I think that's why the paparazzi showed up.
我想这就是狗仔队出现的原因。

1665
01:16:57.260 --> 01:16:58.160
Maybe so.
也许吧。

1666
01:16:58.360 --> 01:16:58.700
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1667
01:16:59.020 --> 01:17:03.800
Because it was just sort of, what, five years in, out of nowhere, oh, this guy wants pictures.
因为差不多是，什么，五年过去了，突然之间，哦，这家伙想要拍照。

1668
01:17:04.960 --> 01:17:05.840
Yes, exactly.
是的，没错。

1669
01:17:06.240 --> 01:17:11.360
The one other time we had paparazzi show up was when we were shooting on location for
唯一一次有狗仔队出现是在我们外景拍摄

1670
01:17:11.360 --> 01:17:12.300
Jim and Pam's wedding.
吉姆和帕姆的婚礼的时候。

1671
01:17:12.600 --> 01:17:13.260
Oh, yeah.
哦，对。

1672
01:17:13.340 --> 01:17:14.760
Well, that would have been a big, like...
嗯，那应该算是一个很大的……

1673
01:17:14.760 --> 01:17:16.240
That was, like, a big show event.
那就像是剧里的一件大事。

1674
01:17:16.300 --> 01:17:16.540
Yeah, yeah.
对，对。

1675
01:17:16.720 --> 01:17:17.460
Within the show.
在剧里。

1676
01:17:17.640 --> 01:17:20.760
But for the most part, we didn't have any of that stuff.
但大多数时候，我们没有那种东西。

1677
01:17:20.920 --> 01:17:22.020
We didn't, thankfully.
幸好我们没有。

1678
01:17:22.160 --> 01:17:25.600
I'm glad that we were our, just our little tucked away little studio.
我很高兴我们只是我们那个偏僻的小小工作室。

1679
01:17:25.940 --> 01:17:26.680
I agree.
我同意。

1680
01:17:27.260 --> 01:17:32.380
I do think at one point, the paparazzi got a shot of me leaving my trailer with, like,
我确实觉得有一次，狗仔队拍到我离开化妆车，手里拿着，呃，

1681
01:17:32.600 --> 01:17:34.540
my empty lunch plate.
我吃完的空餐盘。

1682
01:17:35.280 --> 01:17:37.340
And it is the moSt...
而那是最……

1683
01:17:37.340 --> 01:17:39.000
That made me, like, short laugh.
那让我忍不住笑出声。

1684
01:17:39.680 --> 01:17:46.520
It is just, like, the most unflattering photo of a person who has finished their lunch.
