我不知道该怎么复述，我甚至听不懂你刚才说的是什么，但我很欣赏

1833
01:24:48.620 --> 01:24:50.000
the science behind it.
它背后的科学。

1834
01:24:50.000 --> 01:24:54.640
When you make a pancake, just know there's a lot of physics at work.
当你做煎饼时，只要知道有很多物理学原理在起作用就行了。

1835
01:24:55.020 --> 01:24:55.220
Yeah.
对。

1836
01:24:55.500 --> 01:24:55.720
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1837
01:24:56.180 --> 01:25:01.080
I mean, listen, I think that if you memorize what I said, and you're making pancakes for
我的意思是，听着，我觉得如果你把我说的话背下来，下次你给

1838
01:25:01.080 --> 01:25:05.020
your kids next time, and you just throw that out there, you're going to sound pretty smart.
你的孩子们做煎饼时，随口说出这些，你会显得非常有学问。

1839
01:25:05.980 --> 01:25:07.160
I'll get it wrong.
我会说错的。

1840
01:25:07.580 --> 01:25:08.840
They'll call me on it.
他们会质问我的。

1841
01:25:09.140 --> 01:25:09.600
They'll be like, what are you talking about?
他们会说，你在胡说八道什么呢？

1842
01:25:09.600 --> 01:25:10.740
You have to write it on your hand.
你得把它写在手上。

1843
01:25:10.900 --> 01:25:11.300
I know.
我知道。

1844
01:25:11.420 --> 01:25:12.100
Or on a card.
或者写在卡片上。

1845
01:25:12.260 --> 01:25:13.220
I need a cue card.
我需要一张提示卡。

1846
01:25:13.400 --> 01:25:15.020
Which brings me to...
这让我想到了……

1847
01:25:15.020 --> 01:25:15.580
Oh!
哦！

1848
01:25:15.800 --> 01:25:16.180
Hello!
嗨！

1849
01:25:16.540 --> 01:25:17.860
Such a great scene.
多么棒的一场戏。

1850
01:25:18.300 --> 01:25:20.600
Andy and Dwight in the break room.
安迪和德怀特在休息室里。

1851
01:25:20.880 --> 01:25:28.240
Andy's playing banjo, and Dwight is playing guitar, and they are jamming to Take Me Home
安迪在弹班卓琴，德怀特在弹吉他，他们正在即兴演奏《带我回家》

1852
01:25:28.240 --> 01:25:32.720
Country Road, as Erin looks on, impressed.
乡村路，艾琳看着，印象深刻。

1853
01:25:33.040 --> 01:25:33.480
Oh, yeah.
哦，是的。

1854
01:25:33.560 --> 01:25:36.120
They're really trying to one-up each other in front of her.
他们真的很想在她面前一较高下。

1855
01:25:36.400 --> 01:25:38.040
And she sings along.
而她也跟着唱了起来。

1856
01:25:38.340 --> 01:25:38.740
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1857
01:25:38.900 --> 01:25:39.780
It's amazing.
太棒了。

1858
01:25:40.500 --> 01:25:42.620
We got so much fan mail about this.
我们收到了很多关于这集的粉丝来信。

1859
01:25:43.100 --> 01:25:46.080
Abby Kay wanted to know, was any of this improvised?
艾比·凯想知道，这里面有即兴发挥吗？

1860
01:25:46.140 --> 01:25:49.080
Because Erin looks genuinely shocked when they start singing.
因为当他们开始唱歌时，艾琳看起来真的很震惊。

1861
01:25:49.740 --> 01:25:54.480
And then Jasper D wants to know, does Rain actually play the guitar in real life, or
然后贾斯珀·D想知道，雷恩现实生活中真的会弹吉他吗，还是说

1862
01:25:54.480 --> 01:25:56.380
did he have to learn it just for this scene?
他只是为了这场戏才去学的？

1863
01:25:56.580 --> 01:25:58.680
Well, first of all, this was all planned.
嗯，首先，这一切都是计划好的。

1864
01:25:58.680 --> 01:25:59.860
It was all scripted.
全是按剧本演的。

1865
01:25:59.980 --> 01:26:00.260
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1866
01:26:00.500 --> 01:26:06.240
In fact, Randy Cordray told us that it cost $22,000 to license the song for this scene.
事实上，兰迪·科德雷告诉我们，这场戏购买这首歌的版权花了两万两千美元。

1867
01:26:06.700 --> 01:26:08.640
Also, Rain does play guitar.
另外，雷恩确实会弹吉他。

1868
01:26:08.860 --> 01:26:10.260
He also plays the druMs.
他还打鼓。

1869
01:26:10.840 --> 01:26:12.160
And the recorder.
还有竖笛。

1870
01:26:12.840 --> 01:26:14.580
And the recorder, which we know.
还有竖笛，这个我们都知道。

1871
01:26:15.040 --> 01:26:16.140
And the bassoon.
还有大管。

1872
01:26:16.480 --> 01:26:17.240
Oh, my gosh.
哦，天哪。

1873
01:26:17.240 --> 01:26:18.880
He plays a lot of instruments.
他会演奏很多乐器。

1874
01:26:19.780 --> 01:26:20.980
He can also juggle.
他还会玩杂耍。

1875
01:26:21.220 --> 01:26:22.040
He's a great juggler.
他是个很棒的杂耍艺人。

1876
01:26:22.240 --> 01:26:24.160
He's like a renaissance fear guy.
他就像是个文艺复兴式的恐惧达人。

1877
01:26:24.440 --> 01:26:25.140
He is.
确实是。

1878
01:26:25.240 --> 01:26:26.340
Didn't he go to clown school?
他不是上过小丑学校吗？

1879
01:26:27.180 --> 01:26:28.860
I'm pretty sure he did.
我敢肯定他去过。

1880
01:26:29.020 --> 01:26:29.900
I'm pretty sure he did.
我敢肯定他去过。

1881
01:26:29.920 --> 01:26:30.680
I'm going to say that sounds right.
我觉得这听起来没错。

1882
01:26:30.780 --> 01:26:31.000
Okay.
好吧。

1883
01:26:31.680 --> 01:26:33.380
Well, Ed really does play the banjo.
嗯，艾德确实会弹班卓琴。

1884
01:26:33.600 --> 01:26:37.680
In fact, Ed started a bluegrass band in college called The Lonesome Trio.
事实上，艾德在大学里组建过一个名叫“孤独三人组”的蓝草乐队。

1885
01:26:38.380 --> 01:26:40.560
Ed can play banjo guitar and piano.
艾德会弹班卓琴、吉他和钢琴。

1886
01:26:40.960 --> 01:26:46.300
And these guys, they just practiced together at lunch on the day of the scene to get this right.
而这两个家伙，他们在拍戏当天午休时一起练习，把这首歌练好。

1887
01:26:46.740 --> 01:26:47.180
Yeah.
对。

1888
01:26:47.180 --> 01:26:49.520
You know, when they were filming it, everything was going well.
你知道，他们拍摄的时候，一切都很顺利。

1889
01:26:49.680 --> 01:26:55.420
And then they got to the part where Rain had to sing Take Me Home Country Road in German.
然后到了雷恩必须用德语唱《带我回乡村路》的那部分。

1890
01:26:55.960 --> 01:27:02.620
And something about having to do it in German and keep the tune and play the guitar while Ed's playing.
而且要在用德语唱的同时保持音准，还要一边弹吉他，旁边艾德也在弹。

1891
01:27:02.840 --> 01:27:04.780
He was struggling a little bit.
他有点吃力。

1892
01:27:04.780 --> 01:27:11.720
So Randy said they got him really big cue cards and they wrote out the German part of the lyrics phonetically.
所以兰迪说他们给他准备了非常大的提示板，把德语歌词按发音拼写写了上去。

1893
01:27:12.000 --> 01:27:14.900
They had hired a translator to translate the song.
他们曾雇佣了一位翻译来翻译这首歌。

1894
01:27:15.080 --> 01:27:15.300
Oh, yeah.
哦，是的。

1895
01:27:15.400 --> 01:27:17.660
He's really singing the lyrics in German.
他是真的在用德语唱歌词。

1896
01:27:17.840 --> 01:27:18.020
Yeah.
对。

1897
01:27:18.220 --> 01:27:23.660
They put these huge cue cards right behind Ellie's shoulder just off camera.
他们把这些巨大的提示板放在艾莉肩膀后面正对镜头外的地方。

1898
01:27:24.040 --> 01:27:29.940
And I want you to know, if you go to 17 minutes, 47 seconds, Rain, right in that moment, I see you look at the cue card.
我想让你们知道，如果你看到17分47秒，雷恩，就在那一刻，我看到你看了提示板。

1899
01:27:30.140 --> 01:27:31.000
You see him check it?
你看到他瞄了一眼吗？

1900
01:27:31.120 --> 01:27:31.280
Yeah.
对。

1901
01:27:32.120 --> 01:27:33.500
I mean, that is hard.
我是说，那真的很难。

1902
01:27:33.680 --> 01:27:36.580
It's hard to sing a song you know in another language.
用另一种语言唱你熟悉的歌很难。

1903
01:27:36.580 --> 01:27:40.640
But also, it's a song you just learned on the guitar.
而且，这还是你刚在吉他上学会的歌。

1904
01:27:40.860 --> 01:27:41.000
Yeah.
是啊。

1905
01:27:41.240 --> 01:27:43.840
I remember one Christmas song I learned in Indonesian.
我记得我学过一首印尼语的圣诞歌。

1906
01:27:44.880 --> 01:27:46.560
Selamat Hari Natal.
圣诞快乐。

1907
01:27:46.900 --> 01:27:48.600
Selamat Hari Natal.
圣诞快乐。

1908
01:27:49.040 --> 01:27:50.880
Selamat Hari Natal.
圣诞快乐。

1909
01:27:51.000 --> 01:27:52.520
Danta un baru.
新年快乐。

1910
01:27:53.040 --> 01:27:55.160
We wish you a Merry Christmas.
我们祝你圣诞快乐。

1911
01:27:55.480 --> 01:27:56.060
Nice.
不错。

1912
01:27:56.580 --> 01:27:58.340
You guys know I grew up in Jakarta.
大家知道我是在雅加达长大的。

1913
01:27:58.340 --> 01:28:04.900
But there were times when you would learn a very sort of westernized song in a different language.
但有时你会用另一种语言去学一首很西化的歌。

1914
01:28:05.480 --> 01:28:14.400
Well, did you notice that when Rain is singing in English, he actually gets the lyrics a little wrong?
嘿，你们有没有注意到，当Rain用英文唱歌时，他的歌词其实记错了一点？

1915
01:28:14.400 --> 01:28:14.860
Yeah, yeah.
对，对。

1916
01:28:14.860 --> 01:28:15.600
He flipped it.
他给颠倒过来了。

1917
01:28:15.720 --> 01:28:16.280
He did.
没错。

1918
01:28:16.300 --> 01:28:19.700
So, the real lyrics are, country roads, take me home.
所以，真正的歌词是“乡村路，带我回家”。

1919
01:28:20.480 --> 01:28:23.920
But Rain sings, take me home, country roads.
但Rain唱的是“带我回家，乡村路”。

1920
01:28:24.060 --> 01:28:24.260
Right.
没错。

1921
01:28:24.600 --> 01:28:26.640
Well, I just thought we had to hear this.
我只是觉得我们必须听听这个。

1922
01:28:26.640 --> 01:28:30.780
Can we hear Ed playing the banjo and Rain playing the guitar?
我们能听听Ed弹班卓琴、Rain弹吉他吗？

1923
01:28:31.720 --> 01:28:35.140
Take me home, country road.
带我回家，乡村路。

1924
01:28:36.020 --> 01:28:37.060
To the place.
去那个地方。

1925
01:28:44.750 --> 01:28:47.790
Take me home, country road.
带我回家，乡村路。

1926
01:28:59.680 --> 01:29:00.880
You have to stop.
你得停下了。

1927
01:29:02.060 --> 01:29:04.040
How fun is it to hear those guys play?
听他们弹奏多有意思啊？

1928
01:29:04.240 --> 01:29:07.140
Well, I know they must have had so much fun doing that.
我知道他们当时肯定玩得非常开心。

1929
01:29:07.340 --> 01:29:11.860
I loved listening to it because it made me just think of them in real life.
我特别喜欢听，因为这让我想起了他们在现实生活中的样子。

1930
01:29:12.400 --> 01:29:12.920
Yeah.
是啊。

1931
01:29:13.280 --> 01:29:15.000
The only thing missing for me was Creed.
对我来说唯一的遗憾是少了一个克里德（Creed）。

1932
01:29:15.260 --> 01:29:17.640
Because, you know, Creed would have just been jamming on his mandolin.
因为你知道的，克里德本来可以用他的曼陀林一起即兴演奏的。

1933
01:29:17.960 --> 01:29:19.320
I just loved that moment.
我太喜欢那个时刻了。

1934
01:29:19.680 --> 01:29:25.920
One of the things I also loved was Justin said that, you know, this really showed the bromance.
我喜欢的一点是，贾斯汀（Justin）说这真的展现了兄弟情。

1935
01:29:26.080 --> 01:29:29.560
Because while the beginning, they're trying to one-up each other in their playing.
因为在一开始，他们都在演奏上试图胜过对方。

1936
01:29:29.680 --> 01:29:31.240
And they're playing over each other.
而且他们的演奏声音互相盖过。

1937
01:29:31.460 --> 01:29:33.860
It ends up in just a bromance.
但最终变成了纯粹的兄弟情。

1938
01:29:34.040 --> 01:29:35.760
Mutual admiration club.
互相欣赏俱乐部。

1939
01:29:35.780 --> 01:29:36.880
And Erin's not even there.
而且艾琳（Erin）甚至都不在那里。

1940
01:29:36.880 --> 01:29:38.180
She walks away.
她走开了。

1941
01:29:38.180 --> 01:29:41.880
And now they're just looking at each other, harmonizing and jamming out.
现在他们只是看着彼此，和声并即兴狂欢。

1942
01:29:42.140 --> 01:29:43.620
And they're back.
他们又回来了。

1943
01:29:43.860 --> 01:29:52.920
Well, while I was researching this episode, I found this really cool quote from Ed where he talked about Andy's banjo playing on the show.
嗯，我在为这一集做资料搜集时，发现了Ed关于安迪在剧中弹班卓琴的一句超酷的名言。

1944
01:29:52.920 --> 01:29:55.240
It's from an e-magazine article.
它出自一篇电子杂志文章。

1945
01:29:55.560 --> 01:29:56.820
And here's what he said.
他是这么说的。

1946
01:29:57.000 --> 01:29:57.780
He said,
他说：

1947
01:29:57.780 --> 01:30:01.200
I'm happy to play my banjo at any opportunity I can get.
只要有机会，我随时都乐意弹我的班卓琴。

1948
01:30:01.280 --> 01:30:05.060
But there's no real explanation why Andy plays the banjo.
但对于安迪为什么会弹班卓琴，并没有什么真正的解释。

1949
01:30:05.260 --> 01:30:06.860
It's so fun and weird.
这既有趣又古怪。

1950
01:30:06.860 --> 01:30:08.880
But he's a Connecticut preppy guy.
但他是个康涅狄格州的预科生。

1951
01:30:09.060 --> 01:30:10.480
How did he pick up a banjo?
他怎么会学会弹班卓琴的呢？

1952
01:30:10.720 --> 01:30:12.720
It's one of Andy's many mysteries.
这是安迪身上无数谜团之一。

1953
01:30:13.000 --> 01:30:15.020
Not all of which I even understand.
其中有些连我都搞不懂。

1954
01:30:16.220 --> 01:30:19.480
But I love that Andy plays the banjo.
但我很高兴安迪会弹班卓琴。

1955
01:30:19.620 --> 01:30:20.840
But Ed is so right.
不过埃德说得太对了。

1956
01:30:21.060 --> 01:30:25.560
Like, I never thought, how or why does Andy know how to play the banjo?
比如说，我从没想过，安迪是怎么或为什么会弹班卓琴的？

1957
01:30:25.660 --> 01:30:27.100
Yeah, it doesn't clock at all.
对啊，完全说不通。

1958
01:30:27.180 --> 01:30:29.860
And also that he could just pick up a sitar and play it.
而且他居然能随手拿起一把西塔尔琴弹奏。

1959
01:30:29.860 --> 01:30:30.300
You know?
你知道吗？

1960
01:30:30.420 --> 01:30:32.120
It's like he's so musically talented.
就好像他极具音乐天赋一样。

1961
01:30:32.200 --> 01:30:33.860
I get the acapella side.
阿卡贝拉无伴奏合唱这块我能理解。

1962
01:30:33.960 --> 01:30:36.000
But this banjo is so specific.
但这个班卓琴就太奇特了。

1963
01:30:36.200 --> 01:30:36.620
It is.
确实如此。

1964
01:30:37.140 --> 01:30:41.880
Well, sad to say, the pancake brunch was a little bit of a wash.
嗯，遗憾的是，煎饼早午餐会有点泡汤了。

1965
01:30:42.100 --> 01:30:42.460
Yeah.
是啊。

1966
01:30:42.460 --> 01:30:45.120
Other than the one dude, I don't think anyone came.
除了那家伙，我觉得没人来。

1967
01:30:45.260 --> 01:30:45.880
Creed and Meredith.
克里德和梅雷迪思。

1968
01:30:46.080 --> 01:30:46.500
That's it.
就他们俩。

1969
01:30:46.700 --> 01:30:46.880
Yeah.
对。

1970
01:30:47.360 --> 01:30:51.620
At 18 minutes, 22 seconds, we have a very sad shot of Michael.
在第18分22秒，我们有一个迈克尔非常悲伤的镜头。

1971
01:30:51.900 --> 01:30:55.200
And the wind is blowing the paper all over.
风把纸吹得到处都是。

1972
01:30:56.120 --> 01:31:01.360
Randy told me that we set up huge special effects fans to create this wind.
兰迪告诉我，我们安放了巨大的特效风扇来制造这阵风。

1973
01:31:02.040 --> 01:31:05.420
That it would make the whole thing feel even sadder.
说这样会让整个场面感觉更加悲伤。

1974
01:31:05.680 --> 01:31:10.300
If all these papers were blowing around and the tablecloth was blowing in the wind.
如果所有这些纸都在乱飞，桌布也在风中飘扬的话。

1975
01:31:10.960 --> 01:31:19.960
And then Gene told me that Randall, our cinematographer, spent almost an hour filming paper blowing across the parking lot.
然后吉恩告诉我，我们的摄影师兰德尔花了将近一个小时拍摄纸张在停车场飞舞的镜头。

1976
01:31:20.260 --> 01:31:22.880
Like sad shots of paper blowing.
就像纸张飞舞的悲伤镜头一样。

1977
01:31:23.520 --> 01:31:25.580
He said we never used any of it.
他说我们这些镜头一点都没用上。

1978
01:31:25.640 --> 01:31:27.540
It's an hour of paper blowing footage.
那可是一小时纸张飞舞的素材啊。

1979
01:31:27.640 --> 01:31:28.000
Yes.
没错。

1980
01:31:28.000 --> 01:31:31.760
That would have gone into the closet of tapes.
那些本来都会被塞进磁带储藏室。

1981
01:31:32.060 --> 01:31:32.700
Somewhere.
某个地方。

1982
01:31:33.220 --> 01:31:35.540
Which is now Michael Scott Paper Company.
也就是现在的迈克尔·斯科特纸业公司。

1983
01:31:35.940 --> 01:31:38.460
Well, now they're all really down in the dumps.
好吧，现在他们真的很沮丧。

1984
01:31:38.580 --> 01:31:41.040
They go back into their tiny closet office.
他们回到了他们那狭小的储藏室办公室。

1985
01:31:41.400 --> 01:31:43.640
And you kind of feel like they're giving up.
你会觉得他们快要放弃了。

1986
01:31:43.920 --> 01:31:45.820
And then the phone rings.
然后电话响了。

1987
01:31:46.240 --> 01:31:48.140
And Pam answers it.
帕姆接了电话。

1988
01:31:49.180 --> 01:31:50.500
And guess what?
你猜怎么着？

1989
